---
import Docs from "../layouts/Docs.astro";
import Code from "../components/Code.astro";
---

<Docs
  title="Installation"
  description="Install Clink once to get the command-line client and the MCP server. You can check the installation before connecting an agent."
  toc={[
    ["with-uv", "Install with uv"],
    ["verify", "Verify the installation"],
    ["requirements", "Compatibility"],
  ]}
>
  <h2 id="with-uv">Install with uv</h2>
  <p>
    With{" "}
    <a href="https://docs.astral.sh/uv/getting-started/installation/">
      uv installed
    </a>
    , run the following command. It installs the published Python package into
    an isolated environment.
  </p>
  <Code label="Terminal" code="uv tool install clink-cli" />
  <p>
    If your shell cannot find the new commands, follow uv’s printed PATH
    instructions and start a new shell. If you installed the original v0.2.0
    GitHub wheel with uv, remove its old distribution first with{" "}
    <code>uv tool uninstall clink-mcp-server</code>.
  </p>
  <h2 id="verify">Verify the installation</h2>
  <Code
    label="Terminal"
    code={"clink --help\nclink generation-capabilities --json"}
  />
  <p>
    The second command reports supported generation schemas and agent families.
    It reads local capability information without calling a model. The{" "}
    <a href="/quick-start/#claude">Claude Code quick start</a> verifies the
    separate MCP entry point.
  </p>
  <h2 id="requirements">Compatibility</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Python 3.10 or newer. The project tests against Python 3.12.</li>
    <li>
      Process supervision targets POSIX systems. Recorded native admissions
      cover exact macOS arm64 executables and launch recipes.
    </li>
    <li>
      Sign in through the chosen native CLI before a model call. Native Windows
      delegation is unavailable.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    For a wheel or source installation, follow the{" "}
    <a href="https://github.com/acebytes/clink-cli#install-and-connect">
      upstream installation guide
    </a>
    .
  </p>
</Docs>
